# Kitted API — Category Endpoints
#
# SETUP (do this once before running any request):
#
#   1. Start the server:       go run main.go
#   2. Generate a token:       go run scripts/gen_token.go
#   3. Paste the output below into @token
#
# Recommended order: run the requests top-to-bottom.
# The PATCH and DELETE "happy path" requests use the response captured from
# the POST that creates a category — send that POST first.

@host  = http://localhost:8080
@token =


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  GET /categories
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — returns system + own categories as a flat list
GET {{host}}/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 🔒 401 — no token
GET {{host}}/categories


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  POST /categories
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 201 — creates a new user-owned category
# @name createCategory
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "My Test Category"
}

###

### ❌ 400 — missing name field
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{}

###

### ❌ 400 — empty name
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": ""
}

###

### ❌ 400 — name exceeds 100 characters
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaX"
}

###

### ❌ 409 — duplicate name (requires the 201 above to have been sent first)
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "My Test Category"
}

###

### ✅ 201 — same name as a system category is allowed for user-owned categories
#          (requires seed data: go psql $DATABASE_URL -f db/seeds/categories.sql)
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Toiletries"
}

###

### 🔒 401 — no token
POST {{host}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Should Fail"
}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  PATCH /categories/:id
#
#  The happy-path requests below use the ID captured from the "createCategory"
#  POST above. Send that request first, then run these.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 200 — renames the created category
PATCH {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "My Renamed Category"
}

###

### ✅ 200 — same name as current is a no-op (allowed)
PATCH {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "My Renamed Category"
}

###

### ❌ 400 — empty name
PATCH {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": ""
}

###

### ❌ 400 — name too long
PATCH {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaX"
}

###

### ❌ 404 — category does not exist
PATCH {{host}}/categories/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Anything"
}

###

### 🔒 401 — no token
PATCH {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Should Fail"
}


# ══════════════════════════════════════════
#  DELETE /categories/:id
#
#  Send the createCategory POST first to get an ID to delete.
#  After the 204 below the category is gone — subsequent PATCH/DELETE
#  requests against the same ID will return 404.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════

### ✅ 204 — deletes the created category (no response body)
DELETE {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ❌ 404 — already deleted (or never existed)
DELETE {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### ❌ 404 — non-existent UUID
DELETE {{host}}/categories/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 🔒 401 — no token
DELETE {{host}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
